# Media and derived artefacts — never committed.
raw/
survey/

# `work/` is ignored because it holds the footage: clips of somebody else's
# broadcast, which docs/10-getting-the-footage.md says not to redistribute.
#
# **What a human typed is not footage.** Four files in there are pure human
# input - field coordinates, timestamps, and which end a team attacked - and
# every one of them is the thing this project is least able to regenerate. AD-6
# says the correction log is the highest-value training data it can produce and
# that no public dataset of hand-verified field positions in ultimate exists;
# docs/30 section 2.8 is about a release that quietly threw away tagging
# somebody had been paid to do. All of it was ignored, so a fresh clone had none
# of it and a lost laptop had none of it either.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file under an excluded directory, so the exclusion has
# to be written a file at a time rather than as `work/`.
work/*
!work/*/
work/*/*
!work/*/corrections.json
!work/*/events.json
!work/*/calibration_truth.json
!work/*/identities.json
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Viewer data, regenerated from work/ by tools/make_view.py
viewer/live-data.js

# Local preview convenience; the viewer itself needs no server.
.claude/launch.json

# Renders - regenerable from verify.py / overlay.py / m3_render.py / m4_render.py,
# and they are the broadcast with overlays drawn on it.
*.mp4
*.webm
# ...except the published site, which deliberately carries one clip per
# published possession. See tools/build_site.py for what that publishes
# and how to unpublish one.
!docs/**/*.mp4
